x676c: implement versioned Mali-G57 JM memory and submission transport

Replace the universal-success user client and raw MMIO mapping with per-task
pinned BOs, GPU address spaces, explicit cache ownership, serialized JM jobs,
and actual completion/fault/timeout status. Preserve DMA backing on failed
reset. Use the exact MT6789 r0p1 vendor MMU and initialization definitions and
Mesa v9 descriptor layouts. Normal non-cacheable BOs support ordinary CPU RAM
accesses; another context can allocate and release while a GPU job runs.

Replace the legacy PWRAP protocol with the shared SWINF helper from the X676C
input patch. Preserve firmware voltage selectors; enable rails in vendor order
and verify readback before allowing submission. The shared helper's source and
BSD build entry are supplied by the input patch, not duplicated here.

Hardware execution remains unvalidated. This change has compiled locally to
arm64 XNU objects but has not been flashed or run.

